ld',29,1,' pending '),(4230,'filename',0,1,' certificate of training docx '),(4229,'title',0,1,' basic introduction to locksmithing '),(4230,'kind',0,1,' word '),(4229,'field',70,1,' 0 '),(4230,'extension',0,1,' docx '),(4229,'slug',0,1,' basic introduction to locksmithing '),(4229,'field',150,1,' 0 '),(4229,'field',40,1,''),(4229,'field',49,1,' 0 '),(4229,'field',130,1,' 1 '),(4229,'field',74,1,''),(4229,'field',192,1,''),(4229,'field',194,1,''),(4229,'field',37,1,''),(4096,'field',166,1,' fbaass cpd '),(4096,'field',38,1,' 10 '),(4096,'field',2,1,''),(4096,'field',68,1,' 0 '),(4096,'title',0,1,' business management skills update '),(4096,'slug',0,1,' business management skills '),(4097,'field',166,1,' fbaass cpd '),(4097,'field',38,1,' 5 '),(4097,'field',2,1,''),(4097,'field',68,1,' 0 '),(4097,'title',0,1,' existing technical skills update '),(4097,'slug',0,1,' technical skills '),(4098,'field',166,1,' fbaass cpd '),(4098,'field',38,1,' 0 '),(4098,'field',2,1,''),(4098,'field',68,1,' 0 '),(4098,'title',0,1,' new technical skills development '),(4098,'slug',0,1,' new technical skills update '),(4099,'field',25,1,''),(4099,'field',20,1,''),(4099,'slug',0,1,''),(4100,'field',25,1,''),(4100,'field',20,1,''),(4100,'slug',0,1,''),(4101,'field',25,1,''),(4101,'field',20,1,''),(4101,'slug',0,1,''),(4103,'field',115,1,''),(4103,'field',112,1,' what is cpd cpd stands for continuous professional development this is the continuous progression that helps you maintain and improve your competence used appropriately cpd will provide you with increased skills that can be put into practice for the benefit of your clients cpd is not just about attending training courses it is something that can be carried out every day through structured reading networking and other such activities why is cpd necessary as a member of skills you have agreed to undertake a programme of cpd to ensure that you keep your skills current it is part of the quality assurance that gives your clients confidence in your abilities and illustrates to them the currency of your knowledge how much cpd do i have to do there is no maximum number of points to be attained however a minimum of 20 cpd points annually is required 10 of these points must be in business management and 5 must be in your existing area of technical expertise a summary can be seen of the front of your record card how is cpd measured there are many methods of measuring cpd activity this scheme is based on a points system depending upon the method of learning and the hours undertaken points are rewarded for each cps activity a summary can be seen of the front of your record card how is cpd evidencedthe record card acts as a log of your activities over your membership year where possible a signature should be attained by an appropriate third party to evidence the activity photocopies of certificates and other similar methods of evidence will also be accepted please forward evidence to support your cpd activity with your record card at renewal time what happens of i do not attain 20 cpd pointsyou will not be eligible for re registration unless 20 points have been attained can cpd points be carried into the next membership year no points cannot be carried forward how do i know if an activity qualifies for cpd pointsas cpd is under your control you should ensure that the activity is meaningful and for the benefit of you and your clients points can be gained from many different sources continuous professional development guidance notes '),(4103,'field',2,1,' cpd guidance notes '),(4103,'slug',0,1,' cpd guidance notes for fbass '),(4103,'title',0,1,' cpd guidance notes '),(4104,'field',113,1,' continuous professional development guidance notes '),(4104,'field',114,1,' what is cpd cpd stands for continuous professional development this is the continuous progression that helps you maintain and improve your competence used appropriately cpd will provide you with increased skills that can be put into practice for the benefit of your clients cpd is not just about attending training courses it is something that can be carried out every day through structured reading networking and other such activities why is cpd necessary as a member of skills you have agreed to undertake a programme of cpd to ensure that you keep your skills current it is part of the quality assurance that gives your clients confidence in your abilities and illustrates to them the currency of your knowledge how much cpd do i have to do there is no maximum number of points to be attained however a minimum of 20 cpd points annually is required 10 of these points must be in business management and 5 must be in your existing area of technical expertise a summary can be seen of the front of your record card how is cpd measured there are many methods of measuring cpd activity this scheme is based on a points system depending upon the method of learning and the hours undertaken points are rewarded for each cps activity a summary can be seen of the front of your record card how is cpd evidencedthe record card acts as a log of your activities over your membership year where possible a signature should be attained by an appropriate third party to evidence the activity photocopies of certificates and other similar methods of evidence will also be accepted please forward evidence to support your cpd activity with your record card at renewal time what happens of i do not attain 20 cpd pointsyou will not be eligible for re registration unless 20 points have been attained can cpd points be carried into the next membership year no points cannot be carried forward how do i know if an activity qualifies for cpd pointsas cpd is under your control you should ensure that the activity is meaningful and for the benefit of you and your clients points can be gained from many different sources '),(4104,'slug',0,1,''),(4105,'field',2,1,''),(4105,'field',68,1,' 0 '),(4105,'field',38,1,' 10 '),(4105,'field',166,1,' fbaass cpd '),(4105,'fiel